Theorem RL-23: KnownSafe flag propagation at joins (AND across predecessors)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-23 governs KnownSafe join propagation per Annex E §AIMS
      KnownSafe Pair Elimination: "KnownSafe flag propagation at joins: true
      only if ALL predecessors agree."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - RL-23 is the dataflow-merge rule for the RL-22 KnownSafe flag; it is a
      POST-PIPELINE pass over realized IR.
    - depends-on RL-22 (the KnownSafe flag definition).

  Soundness property:
    Forall CFG join J with predecessor KnownSafe flags p_1, ..., p_n:

      (P1) Join value: KnownSafe(J) = AND(p_1, ..., p_n) — true iff EVERY
           predecessor is KnownSafe.

      (P2) Soundness: if ANY predecessor lacks the outstanding logical owner-
           credit evidence, pair removal is not proven to preserve the later
           owner-credit floor. The conservative AND-join therefore marks J NOT
           KnownSafe. An OR-join would UNSOUNDLY import evidence from one
           predecessor onto a path where it was never established.

    RL-23 is the meet operation that keeps the RL-22 elimination sound across
    control-flow merges.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1) — AND-join grid:
      all_preds_safe_join_safe -> true
      one_pred_unsafe_join_unsafe -> false
      all_preds_unsafe_join_unsafe -> false
      single_safe_pred_safe -> true
      Coverage gate: 4 join cases.

    Part (P2) — AND-not-OR witness:
      The verifier confirms the join uses AND (conservative), not OR: an
      OR-join over [true, false] would yield true (unsound), while the
      required AND-join yields false. The negative-direction witness asserts
      AND is used (the OR result is rejected as the join semantics).

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY —
        section_08::verify_rl23_knownsafe_join_propagation; AND-join
        enumeration + AND-not-OR witness; emits Fail on a wrong join value or
        OR-join semantics)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-23 via the KnownSafe AND-join grid (any unsafe predecessor -> unsafe join) with a negative-direction witness confirming AND (conservative meet), not OR, is the join semantics — keeping RL-22 elimination sound across CFG merges
